---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Bug1 = `function greet() {
  console.log("Welcome aboard.");
}

greet;`;
const Bug2 = `function double(n) {
  n * 2;
}

console.log(double(8));`;
const Bug3 = `function crewLine(name, role) {
  console.log(name + " - " + role);
}

crewLine("Avery", "Pilot");
crewLine("Engineer", "Blake");`;
const Bug4 = `function total(a, b) {
  return a + b;
}

console.log(total(3, 4));
console.log(Total(5, 6));`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: Procedures</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>Four short programs about defining and calling. Every one of them is about the boundary between writing a procedure and running it.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Three kinds of mistake.</b> A <b class="text-sn-red">syntax
            error</b> stops the program before it runs. A{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-orange">reference error</b> runs until it hits the
            bad name, so you get partial output and then a crash. A{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-yellow">logic error</b> runs cleanly and gives the
            wrong answer.
          </p>

          <p><b>Three of these four are logic errors.</b></p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bugs">
          <h2>The Four Programs</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 1</h3>

          <p>This should print a greeting. Nothing appears, and there is no error.</p>

          <Code code={Bug1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 1" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 2</h3>

          <p>This should print the doubled value. It prints <code>undefined</code>.</p>

          <Code code={Bug2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 2" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 3</h3>

          <p>This should print a crew line for each person. The second call prints nonsense.</p>

          <Code code={Bug3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 3" class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Also:</b> There is no error message here. Say what would have to be true of JavaScript for it to catch this.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 4</h3>

          <p>This crashes. Read the message before you change anything.</p>

          <Code code={Bug4} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 4" class="mb-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>For each program: which kind, one sentence on what was wrong, and the corrected line.</p>

          <p>Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Debugging
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
